Source: libdqrobotics-interface-mujoco
Section: libdevel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Juan José Quiroz Omaña <juanjqogm@gmail.com>
# MuJoCo (and the libraries it builds in) and Dear ImGui (the GUI of the
# viewer, built into the library) are downloaded by CMake's FetchContent
# during the build (dependencies.cmake), so building needs network access
# and ca-certificates for the HTTPS download.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
 dpkg-dev (>= 1.18.11),
 cmake,
 g++,
 ca-certificates,
 libeigen3-dev,
 libdqrobotics,
 libmarinholab-sas-core,
 libglfw3-dev,
 libgl-dev,
 libegl-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/juanjqo/cpp-interface-mujoco

Package: libdqrobotics-interface-mujoco
Architecture: any
# The libraries are shared (upstream's default) and dpkg-shlibdeps finds
# their system dependencies (GLFW, EGL, ...). libdqrobotics and
# libmarinholab-sas-core ship from PPAs (DQ Robotics and SmartArmStack), so
# they are declared here, unversioned. The CMake package needs Eigen's
# headers and marinholab_sas_core's CMake package (find_dependency).
Depends: libdqrobotics,
 libmarinholab-sas-core,
 libeigen3-dev,
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Unofficial DQ Robotics interface for C++17 to interact with MuJoCo
 cpp-interface-mujoco connects DQ Robotics (C++17) to MuJoCo: it loads and
 builds scenes, runs the simulation in real time, and reads and commands
 joints, bodies and cameras with dual quaternions.
 .
 This package ships the libraries, their headers, the CMake package
 dqrobotics-interface-mujoco (targets dqrobotics_extensions::interface-mujoco
 and dqrobotics_extensions::interface-mujoco-generic-robots, and
 dq_mujoco_embed_model()), and the MuJoCo 3.16 shared library it is built
 with (libmujoco.so), with the licenses of MuJoCo and its bundled libraries.
